  "description": "Set up a local Kubernetes development environment using kind, k3d, or minikube for fast inner-loop development. Covers cluster creation, ingress configuration, local registry setup, and integration with development tools like Skaffold and Tilt for automatic rebuild and redeploy workflows. Use when needing a local Kubernetes environment for development, testing manifests or Helm charts before production deployment, wanting fast automatic rebuild-and-redeploy cycles, or learning Kubernetes without cloud costs.",
